「%1$s」佔用了大量處理器（%2$.0f%%）	"%1$s" is using a lot of processor (%2$.0f%%)
它正在拖慢整台電腦。如果不是你想讓它跑的工作，可以結束它；要等它做完的話就先放著。	It is slowing down the whole computer. If it isn't a job you want running, you can quit it; if you want it to finish, leave it alone.
結束「%1$s」	Quit "%1$s"
系統負載偏高（%2$.1f，只有 %3$.0f 個核心）	System load is high (%2$.1f, only %3$.0f cores)
同時在等處理器的工作太多，沒有單一行程特別突出。看看活動監視器裡是哪些程式在忙。	Too many jobs are waiting for the processor at once, and no single process stands out. See which programs are busy in Activity Monitor.
打開活動監視器	Open Activity Monitor
記憶體快用完了（可用只剩 %2$.0f%%）	Memory is almost used up (only %2$.0f%% available)
記憶體不夠時系統會把資料搬到硬碟（交換），所有東西都會變慢。關掉不用的程式，或找出吃記憶體的程式。	When memory runs short, the system moves data to the disk (swap) and everything slows down. Close programs you don't need, or find the memory hog.
「%1$s」佔了 %2$.0f MB 記憶體（約 %3$.0f%%）	"%1$s" uses %2$.0f MB of memory (about %3$.0f%%)
單一程式吃掉大部分記憶體，可能是記憶體洩漏或開了太多分頁。重新啟動這個程式通常會改善。	One program is using most of the memory, possibly a memory leak or too many tabs. Restarting this program usually helps.
正在大量換進換出交換空間（已用 %2$.0f%%）	Heavy swapping in progress (%2$.0f%% used)
實體記憶體不夠，系統一直在記憶體與硬碟之間搬資料，這是最常見的「突然很卡」原因之一。	Physical memory is not enough, so the system keeps shuffling data between memory and disk; this is one of the most common causes of a sudden slowdown.
交換空間用掉 %2$.0f%%（目前沒有在大量搬動）	Swap is %2$.0f%% used (not heavily swapping right now)
以前記憶體吃緊時留下的資料還在交換空間裡，現在不一定會拖慢。要清掉可以重新開機，或之後記憶體又吃緊時再注意。	Data from an earlier memory squeeze is still in swap and may not be slowing things down now. Restart to clear it, or watch again the next time memory runs short.
硬碟忙不過來（I/O 等待 %2$.0f%%）	The disk can't keep up (I/O wait %2$.0f%%)
處理器有很多時間在等硬碟，所有要讀寫檔案的動作都會變慢。看看是不是在複製大量檔案、掃描、備份或更新。	The processor spends a lot of time waiting for the disk, so everything that reads or writes files slows down. Check whether you are copying many files, scanning, backing up or updating.
磁碟快滿了：%1$s 只剩 %2$.0f%%	Disk almost full: %1$s has only %2$.0f%% left
磁碟太滿時系統寫不進暫存檔，程式會變慢甚至當掉。清理不用的檔案、舊的日誌與套件快取。	When the disk is too full the system can't write temporary files, and programs slow down or even crash. Clean up unused files, old logs and the package cache.
清理磁碟空間	Free Up Disk Space
%1$s 的檔案數量快用完了（%2$.0f%%）	%1$s is almost out of file entries (%2$.0f%%)
即使還有空間，檔案數量到上限就不能再建新檔案。找出放了大量小檔案的資料夾（暫存、快取、郵件）清掉。	Even with free space left, no new files can be created once the file count hits the limit. Find the folders holding lots of small files (temp, cache, mail) and clean them.
溫度太高（%2$.0f °C），處理器可能降速了	Temperature is too high (%2$.0f °C); the processor may be slowing down
過熱時處理器會自動降速保護自己，電腦就變慢。清理散熱孔灰塵、放在通風的地方、不要蓋住筆電底部。	When overheated, the processor slows itself down to protect itself, and the computer becomes slow. Clean dust from the vents, keep it somewhere ventilated, and don't cover the bottom of a laptop.
病毒掃描正在進行（%1$s）	Virus scan in progress (%1$s)
掃描會讀整顆硬碟，做的時候電腦會比較慢，做完就恢復。不急的話讓它跑完。	A scan reads the whole disk, so the computer is slower while it runs and recovers afterwards. If it isn't urgent, let it finish.
停止「%1$s」	Stop "%1$s"
系統正在安裝或檢查更新（%1$s）	The system is installing or checking for updates (%1$s)
更新進行中會佔用處理器與硬碟，而且這時候套件管理員被鎖住；等它做完再重新開機最好。	Updates take processor and disk, and the package manager is locked meanwhile; it's best to wait until they finish before restarting.
背景正在建立索引或整理硬碟（%1$s）	Indexing or tidying the disk in the background (%1$s)
這類工作通常幾分鐘到幾十分鐘，做完就恢復；剛裝完系統或新增大量檔案後最常見。	This kind of work usually takes a few minutes to a few dozen minutes and then ends; it's most common right after installing the system or adding many files.
服務一直在重新啟動：%1$s	A service keeps restarting: %1$s
服務啟動失敗、又被系統自動拉起來，這樣反覆會一直消耗處理器與日誌。看看它的日誌找出原因。	A service fails to start and the system keeps bringing it back; this loop keeps using processor and filling logs. Check its log to find the cause.
重新啟動 %1$s	Restart %1$s
%2$.0f 個服務已經失敗（%1$s 等）	%2$.0f services have failed (%1$s and others)
失敗的服務不一定會讓電腦變慢，但表示有東西沒有正常運作。	A failed service doesn't necessarily slow the computer, but it means something isn't working properly.
有很多連線卡住了	Many connections are stuck
大量連線卡在「正在連線」通常是網路不通、DNS 有問題或被防火牆擋住；CLOSE_WAIT 太多表示有程式沒有關閉連線。	Many connections stuck in "connecting" usually mean the network is down, DNS has a problem, or a firewall is blocking; too many CLOSE_WAIT means a program isn't closing its connections.
系統日誌太大（%2$.1f GB）	The system log is too large (%2$.1f GB)
日誌太大會讓查看日誌、開機分析變慢，也佔空間。保留近期的就夠了。	Large logs slow down viewing logs and startup analysis, and take space. Keeping the recent ones is enough.
把日誌縮到 500 MB	Shrink Logs to 500 MB
有更新要重新開機才會生效	Updates need a restart to take effect
更新過的核心與函式庫要重新開機才會生效；很多小問題重新開機就好了。	Updated kernels and libraries only take effect after a restart; many small problems go away with a restart.
電腦已經開機 %2$.0f 天沒有重新開機，記憶體也不寬裕	The computer has been up for %2$.0f days without a restart, and memory is tight
長時間開機後記憶體容易被快取與洩漏佔掉；重新開機一次通常最快。	After a long uptime, memory tends to be taken by caches and leaks; a restart is usually the fastest fix.
它在等網路連上才讓開機繼續；桌面電腦與筆電通常不需要等，可以停用	It waits for the network before letting startup continue; desktops and laptops usually don't need to wait, so it can be disabled
它在等網路連上才讓開機繼續，通常可以停用	It waits for the network before letting startup continue, and can usually be disabled
等開機動畫結束，不是真正的瓶頸	Waits for the boot animation to finish; not a real bottleneck
等所有裝置就緒，現代系統通常不需要	Waits for all devices to be ready; modern systems usually don't need it
雲端主機的初始化，個人電腦通常用不到	Cloud host initialization; personal computers usually don't need it
snap 套件管理程式啟動，裝了很多 snap 時會變慢	The snap package manager starting; it gets slow when many snaps are installed
Docker 啟動；不是每次開機都要用的話可以改成需要時才啟動	Docker starting; if you don't need it at every startup, it can be changed to start on demand
開機後檢查更新	Checking for updates after startup
等待磁碟出現	Waiting for the disk to appear
比平常（約 %.0f 秒）慢了 %.0f 秒	%.0f seconds slower than usual (about %.0f seconds)
跟平常（約 %.0f 秒）差不多	About the same as usual (about %.0f seconds)
這次開機花了 %.0f 秒，比較慢	This startup took %.0f seconds, which is slow
這次開機花了 %.0f 秒	This startup took %.0f seconds
核心 %.1f 秒＋使用者空間 %.1f 秒	Kernel %.1f s + user space %.1f s
看下面拖慢最多的服務；沒有必要的可以停用，有的是在等網路或裝置。	See the services below that slow it down the most; those you don't need can be disabled, and some are just waiting for the network or devices.
開機時間在正常範圍。	Startup time is in the normal range.
開機時「%s」花了 %.0f 秒	"%s" took %.0f seconds during startup
拖慢開機最多的服務之一	One of the services that slow startup the most
用不到的話可以停用，下次開機就不用等。	If you don't use it, you can disable it so the next startup doesn't wait for it.
先弄清楚它在做什麼，再決定要不要延後或停用。	Find out what it does first, then decide whether to delay or disable it.
停用這個服務	Disable This Service
